() Tj T*
(In so far as these pages reflect the thoughts of a busy stockbroker,) Tj T*
(distracted by many duties and lacking in literary skill, they have but) Tj T*
(little merit and the writer entertains no illusions regarding them.) Tj T*
(But in the many quotations from the writings of the world?s foremost) Tj T*
(economists that are here presented, and in the various legal and) Tj T*
(historical precedents cited, perhaps it is not too much to hope that) Tj T*
(this book possesses some slight value as a contribution to the vexed) Tj T*
(and vexing discussion of the Stock Exchange, and that it may serve) Tj T*
(in some degree both to dull the sharp edge of uninformed criticism) Tj T*
(and to strengthen the hands and hearts of loyal friends of a greatly) Tj T*
(misunderstood institution. The public is asked to disregard the) Tj T*
(utterances of demagogues and self-seekers and to consider facts. That) Tj T*
(done, the American spirit of fair play may be confidently relied upon.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Stock Exchange authorities have had no hand in the preparation of) Tj T*
(the work, nor does it bear their endorsement. I say this lest it be) Tj T*
(thought an official _apologia_. Had it been such, the work would have) Tj T*
(been much more skillfully done, and its value greatly enhanced.) Tj T*
