(highest prices; and so it was learned long ago that economy of time and) Tj T*
(labor, as well as a theoretically perfect market, could be best secured) Tj T*
(by an organization under one roof of as many dealers in a commodity as) Tj T*
(could be found.[2] Bear in mind that this result, moreover, is best) Tj T*
(accomplished when the organization is so controlled by rigid rules of) Tj T*
(business morality as to insure to every one who does business there,) Tj T*
(great and small, rich and poor, an absolutely square deal. In such a) Tj T*
(market every purchase is made with the most thorough acquaintance with) Tj T*
(the conditions involved. Each dealer, each broker, each speculator,) Tj T*
(strives to obtain the best knowledge of the supply and demand, and) Tj T*
(the earliest news that may affect it, and each buyer or seller has an) Tj T*
(equal and a fair opportunity to profit by the resultant effect on the) Tj T*
(market of all these various agencies. The larger the body of brokers) Tj T*
(and traders, then, the more accurate the standards of value thus) Tj T*
(created. It is a pity you could not have bought your piano under such) Tj T*
(conditions.[3]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Demagogues have set the agricultural classes against Wall Street and) Tj T*
(against Exchanges, but producers everywhere, in default of exchanges,) Tj T*
(are forming quasi-exchanges of their own. Every day we hear of) Tj T*
(combinations, Farmers? Alliances, rural co-operative movements, etc.,) Tj T*
(each designed to regulate the market for eggs, butter, potatoes, and) Tj T*
(such things, and each having for its purpose the very functions which) Tj T*
(govern a Stock Exchange in its own field--namely, the establishment of) Tj T*
(a fair price under the nearest possible approach to ideal conditions.) Tj T*
(It is now proposed in Congress that the Department of Agriculture) Tj T*
(shall collect and transmit to the agricultural districts by telephone) Tj T*
(and telegraph all available information concerning price movements,) Tj T*
(markets, and centres of supply and demand, this again embodying the) Tj T*
(essential functions performed in its own field by a great exchange.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In practice, of course, there can be no exchange to deal in perishable) Tj T*
(products of the farm, and this is a pity, because if such an exchange) Tj T*
(were practicable we should hear less of our old friend the cost of) Tj T*
(living. Why? Because at present the market for these commodities is) Tj T*
(controlled by commission dealers and by middlemen. The producer and the) Tj T*
(consumer are alike at the mercy of these people; the price is fixed by) Tj T*
(them; the number of bona fide dealers actually bidding against each) Tj T*
(other is limited, in many instances there is no competition whatever;) Tj T*
(the producer and the commission dealer are, moreover, widely separated;) Tj T*
(the man who sells has few sources of information, and it is the) Tj T*
(business of the dealer who buys to see that he gets none; the small) Tj T*
(producer therefore has to submit to a great inequality in price, and) Tj T*
(often to downright cheating. There is no standard. There are no rules) Tj T*
(governing the dealer, and no high-minded board to enforce his honesty.) Tj T*
(Naturally this sort of thing contributes to the cost of living, since) Tj T*
(the commission dealer, on his part, regulates his profits just in) Tj T*
(proportion to the ignorance, cupidity or remoteness of the farmer,) Tj T*
(while the middlemen, of whom there are sometimes three or four, apply) Tj T*
(the same iniquitous processes to the ultimate purchaser--who happens) Tj T*
(to be you or me. Every thinking man knows that this is rank economic) Tj T*
