(A friend of mine owns a thousand-acre farm in the Shenandoah Valley,) Tj T*
(where he raised this year 10,000 baskets of peaches. He decided to seek) Tj T*
(one buyer, and he found him in the person of a Baltimore canner, who) Tj T*
(went down to Virginia, inspected the crop, and contracted for the lot) Tj T*
(on a basis of $1 for firsts, 70 cents for seconds, and 40 cents for) Tj T*
(thirds, delivered at Baltimore. Shortly after, the market was flooded) Tj T*
(with peaches from Georgia, and the Baltimore man, seeing that the) Tj T*
(crop would be plentiful, promptly ?welched? on his trade, basing his) Tj T*
(action on the absurd contention that ?firsts? should be three inches in) Tj T*
(diameter, although as every one knows peaches of this size are almost) Tj T*
(never to be had. This action threw all the grower?s peaches into third) Tj T*
(class, which delivered at Baltimore would have netted him about 10) Tj T*
(cents a basket.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In desperation he looked elsewhere, West, North, and South, only) Tj T*
(to hear the same monotonous answer from commission men, ?we won?t) Tj T*
(buy, but we will handle your crop on a commission of 10 per cent.?) Tj T*
(Meantime the crop was ripening. To make matters worse the railroad) Tj T*
(levied a prohibitive price, and refrigerator cars were not to be had.) Tj T*
(Finally there was nothing left but to ship by express and trust to the) Tj T*
(commission men to treat him honestly. The final accounting showed that) Tj T*
(on his first shipment he netted 5½ cents a basket, and on his second,) Tj T*
(15 cents, not counting the expense of picking, packing, and hauling.) Tj T*
(So much for the producer. The consumer fared no better, for he had to) Tj T*
(pay $1.25 per basket for this fruit; one of this producer?s friends) Tj T*
(actually purchasing a portion of this very consignment at that rate.) Tj T*
(The difference therefore between 15 cents and $1.25 contributes some) Tj T*
(food for thought as to the cost of living.[5]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Now contrast this experience of a grower having no exchange facilities) Tj T*
(with that of the Western farmer who deals directly with a Grain) Tj T*
(Exchange. The farmer can sell his crop, even though it has not been) Tj T*
(planted. Whenever he sells, and under whatever conditions, he enjoys) Tj T*
(the authoritative establishment of a price, fixed as clearly as matters) Tj T*
(are fixed in law. Moreover, the price at which he elects to sell is the) Tj T*
(best price, the fairest price, and the most scientific price that human) Tj T*
(agencies can arrive at, because it is made by world-wide competitive) Tj T*
(bidding at the hands of skilled men in Chicago, in New York, in) Tj T*
(Liverpool, in Berlin, in Odessa, and in the Argentine, all competing by) Tj T*
(cable and telegraph. Think of the confidence he enjoys, and the liberty) Tj T*
(of action; think, too, what it means to him to know that the Exchange) Tj T*
(through which he deals is a body of honorable men, governed by rules,) Tj T*
(bidding publicly under one roof.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
