(is altogether unnecessary. Now, in order to explain the error in this) Tj T*
(point of view, let us first see how bits of paper, called securities,) Tj T*
(came into being.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Long after Europe had emerged from the dark centuries following) Tj T*
(the fall of the Roman Empire, the needs of states and governments) Tj T*
(impelled their rulers to resort to credit, and it was discovered that) Tj T*
(the simplest way to do it was to issue securities, that is to say,) Tj T*
(certificates of the debt. Next, it was found that in order to insure) Tj T*
(success for these operations, a market was required. Intermittent or) Tj T*
(temporary sources from which credit could be obtained was not enough;) Tj T*
(constant sources of credit were essential, and, as these _constant_) Tj T*
(sources lay in the savings of the people, public markets in which) Tj T*
(investors could tell the value of their investments from day to day) Tj T*
(followed as a natural course.[6]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As time went on--necessarily the evolution was gradual--it was learned) Tj T*
(that companies having to do with all forms of business enterprises) Tj T*
(might also be formed on the same basis. The development of the world?s) Tj T*
(business outgrew its infancy days of private partnerships, and) Tj T*
(corporate organization of necessity took their place, now that the) Tj T*
(discovery of credit, through the use of securities, had pointed the) Tj T*
(way. This corporate organization, which combines the small savings) Tj T*
(of thousands into large sums and gives to the masses an intelligent) Tj T*
(directing force at the hands of highly trained experts, depends for its) Tj T*
(existence on the sale of its securities.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In order to understand that there can be no industrial progress without) Tj T*
(the issue of securities let us consider the locomotive engine. When in) Tj T*
(the early 1800?s it became apparent that this contrivance could be used) Tj T*
(to operate an entirely new method of transportation, people looked upon) Tj T*
(it, at first, as an interesting but quite useless contrivance, because) Tj T*
(to build railroads was an expensive undertaking and nobody had enough) Tj T*
(money to finance it. The inventor?s genius was not sufficient; another) Tj T*
(power was necessary to take it out of purely scientific hands and give) Tj T*
(it practical impulse. That power was credit; the way it was obtained) Tj T*
(was through the issue of securities, and the way securities were made) Tj T*
(popular vehicles of investment lay in providing a daily market for) Tj T*
(buyers and sellers.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As a natural result, organization followed. Capital was consolidated,) Tj T*
(the rights of owners were established, a great impulse was given) Tj T*
(to various new forms of inventive genius and powerful commercial) Tj T*
(enterprises of all kinds sprang into being. With this development the) Tj T*
(market-places or Stock Exchanges without which capital could not) Tj T*
(have been enlisted kept pace. It was found that transactions in the) Tj T*
(securities which represented the people?s money should be rendered) Tj T*
(easy, quick, and safe, and that the very essence of the Exchange?s) Tj T*
(functions consisted in protecting the people who were the actual owners) Tj T*
(of the enterprises by rules that would insure this result.) Tj T*
