(when he has ?missed his market,? turns the order over to the specialist) Tj T*
(and shifts the responsibility to his shoulders. This is scarcely fair,) Tj T*
(and it simply should not happen. The customer protests at the delay and) Tj T*
(at the price; he is told the specialist is responsible, and straightway) Tj T*
(another voice joins the chorus that holds the specialist in abhorrence.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Like the chairman of the House Committee of a club, the specialist) Tj T*
(is made to bear everybody?s burdens; he is the target for all the) Tj T*
(criticism that any one chooses to hurl at him. And yet he is one of) Tj T*
(the most useful and indispensable features of the Exchange machinery.) Tj T*
(Without him there would be no market whatever in very many securities;) Tj T*
(like the London jobber, he is constantly on the spot, ready to take) Tj T*
(chances by creating at his personal risk a market where none may have) Tj T*
(existed. If it be urged that the specialist should not speculate, but) Tj T*
(should confine himself solely to executing the orders on his books, it) Tj T*
(may be answered that in such a case he would often be useless, for in) Tj T*
(many instances the orders on his books are insufficient in volume to) Tj T*
(establish a close market or anything approaching it. By reason of his) Tj T*
(speculations a market is created; without them it may not exist. He) Tj T*
(speculates, therefore, for the same reason that jobbers in the London) Tj T*
(market speculate, and dealers in wheat, cotton, and wool. Like them, he) Tj T*
(must have goods on hand to supply the demand, and in the purchase of) Tj T*
(these goods \(securities\) he speculates, legitimately, on the hope or) Tj T*
(belief that buyers will appear.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
