() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THE SUBJECT IN GENERAL) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Markets have sprung into being wherever buying and selling have been) Tj T*
(conducted on a large scale. Taken in charge by regular organizations) Tj T*
(and controlled by rules, such markets become exchanges. In New York) Tj T*
(City there are two exchanges dealing in securities and seven in) Tj T*
(commodities. In addition there is a security market, without fixed) Tj T*
(membership or regular officers, known as the ?Curb.? The exchanges) Tj T*
(dealing in commodities are incorporated, while those dealing in) Tj T*
(securities are not.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Commodities are not held for permanent investment, but are bought) Tj T*
(and sold primarily for the purpose of commercial distribution; on) Tj T*
(the other hand, securities are primarily held for investment; but) Tj T*
(both are subject of speculation. Speculation consists in forecasting) Tj T*
(changes of value and buying or selling in order to take advantage) Tj T*
(of them; it may be wholly legitimate, pure gambling, or something) Tj T*
(partaking of the qualities of both. In some form it is a necessary) Tj T*
(incident of productive operations. When carried on in connection with) Tj T*
(either commodities or securities it tends to steady their prices.) Tj T*
(Where speculation is free, fluctuations in prices, otherwise violent) Tj T*
(and disastrous, ordinarily become gradual and comparatively harmless.) Tj T*
(Moreover, so far as commodities are concerned, in the absence of) Tj T*
(speculation, merchants and manufacturers would themselves be forced to) Tj T*
(carry the risks involved in changes of prices and to bear them in the) Tj T*
(intensified condition resulting from sudden and violent fluctuations in) Tj T*
(value. Risks of this kind which merchants and manufacturers still have) Tj T*
(to assume are reduced in amount, because of the speculation prevailing;) Tj T*
(and many of these milder risks they are enabled, by ?hedging,? to) Tj T*
(transfer to others. For the merchant or manufacturer the speculator) Tj T*
(performs a service which has the effect of insurance.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In law, speculation becomes gambling when the trading which it involves) Tj T*
(does not lead, and is not intended to lead, to the actual passing from) Tj T*
(hand to hand of the property that is dealt in. Thus, in the recent case) Tj T*
