(THE PROBLEM TO BE SOLVED) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The problem, wherever speculation is strongly rooted, is to eliminate) Tj T*
(that which is wasteful and morally destructive, while retaining and) Tj T*
(allowing free play to that which is beneficial. The difficulty in) Tj T*
(the solution of the problem lies in the practical impossibility of) Tj T*
(distinguishing what is virtually gambling from legitimate speculation.) Tj T*
(The most fruitful policy will be found in measures which will lessen) Tj T*
(speculation by persons not qualified to engage in it. In carrying) Tj T*
(out such a policy exchanges can accomplish more than legislatures.) Tj T*
(In connection with our reports on the different exchanges, as well) Tj T*
(as on the field of investment and speculation which lies outside of) Tj T*
(the exchanges, we hall make recommendations directed to the removal) Tj T*
(of various evils now existing and to the reduction of the volume of) Tj T*
(speculation of the gambling type.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THE NEW YORK STOCK EXCHANGE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The New York Stock Exchange is a voluntary association, limited to 1100) Tj T*
(members, of whom about 700 are active, some of them residents of other) Tj T*
(cities. Memberships are sold for about $80,000. The Exchange as such) Tj T*
(does no business, merely providing facilities to members and regulating) Tj T*
(their conduct. The governing power is in an elected committee of forty) Tj T*
(members and is plenary in scope. The business transacted on the floor) Tj T*
(is the purchase and sale of stocks and bonds of corporations and) Tj T*
(governments. Practically all transactions must be completed by delivery) Tj T*
(and payment on the following day.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The mechanism of the Exchange provided by its constitution and) Tj T*
(rules, is the evolution of more than a century. An organization of) Tj T*
(stockbrokers existed here in 1792, acquiring more definite form in) Tj T*
(1817. It seems certain that for a long period the members were brokers) Tj T*
(or agents only; at the present time many are principles as well as) Tj T*
(agents, trading for themselves as well as for their customers. A number) Tj T*
(of prominent capitalists hold memberships merely for the purpose of) Tj T*
(availing themselves of the reduced commission charge which the rules) Tj T*
(authorize between members.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The volume of transactions indicates that the Exchange is to-day) Tj T*
(probably the most important financial institution in the world. In the) Tj T*
(past decade the average annual sales of shares have been 196,500,000 at) Tj T*
(prices involving an annual average turnover of nearly $15,500,000,000;) Tj T*
(bond transactions averaged about $800,000,000. This enormous business) Tj T*
(affects the financial and credit interests of the country in so large) Tj T*
(a measure that its proper regulation is a matter of transcendent) Tj T*
