(general conditions of business. Testimony is clear as to the result) Tj T*
(which, in the long run, attends their operations; commissions and) Tj T*
(interest charges constitute a factor always working against them. Since) Tj T*
(good luck and bad luck alternate in time, the gains only stimulate) Tj T*
(these men to larger ventures, and they persist in them till a serious) Tj T*
(or ruinous loss forces them out of the ?Street.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(5.\) Inexperienced persons, who act on interested advice, ?tips,?) Tj T*
(advertisements in newspapers, or circulars sent by mail, or ?take) Tj T*
(flyers? in absolute ignorance, and with blind confidence in their luck.) Tj T*
(Almost without exception they eventually lose.) Tj T*
