() Tj T*
(MARGIN TRADING) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Purchasing securities on margin is as legitimate a transaction as a) Tj T*
(purchase of any other property in which part payment is deferred. We) Tj T*
(therefore see no reason whatsoever for recommending the radical change) Tj T*
(suggested, that margin trading be prohibited.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Two practices are prolific of losses--namely, buying active securities) Tj T*
(on small margins and buying unsound securities, paying for them in) Tj T*
(full. The losses in the former case are due to the quick turns in the) Tj T*
(market, to which active stocks are subject; these exhaust the margins) Tj T*
(and call for more money than the purchasers can supply. The losses in) Tj T*
(the latter case are largely due to misrepresentations of interested) Tj T*
(parties and unscrupulous manipulations.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To correct the evils of misrepresentation and manipulation, we shall) Tj T*
(offer in another part of this report certain recommendations. In so far) Tj T*
(as losses are due to insufficient margins, they would be materially) Tj T*
(reduced if the customary percentage of margins were increased. The) Tj T*
(amount of margin which a broker requires from a speculative buyer of) Tj T*
(stocks depends, in each case, on the credit of the buyer; and the) Tj T*
(amount of credit which one person may extend to another is a dangerous) Tj T*
(subject on which to legislate. Upon the other hand, a rule made by the) Tj T*
(Exchange could safely deal with the prevalent rate of margins required) Tj T*
(from customers. In preference, therefore, to recommending legislation,) Tj T*
(we urge upon all brokers to discourage speculation upon small margins) Tj T*
(and upon the Exchange to use its influence, and, if necessary, its) Tj T*
(power, to prevent members from soliciting and generally accepting) Tj T*
(business on a less margin than 20 per cent.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(PYRAMIDING) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?Pyramiding,? which is the use of paper profits in stock transactions) Tj T*
(as a margin for further commitments, should be discouraged. The) Tj T*
(practice tends to produce more extreme fluctuations and more rapid) Tj T*
(wiping out of margins. If the stockbrokers and the banks would make it) Tj T*
(a rule to value securities for the purpose of margin or collateral, not) Tj T*
(at the current price of the moment, but at the average price of, say,) Tj T*
(the previous two or three months \(provided that such average price were) Tj T*
(not higher than the price of the moment\), the dangers of pyramiding) Tj T*
(would be largely prevented.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SHORT SELLING) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(We have been strongly urged to advise the prohibition or limitation) Tj T*
(of short sales, not only on the theory that it is wrong to agree to) Tj T*
