(MANIPULATION OF PRICES) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A subject to which we have devoted much time and thought is that of the) Tj T*
(manipulation of prices by large interests. This falls into two general) Tj T*
(classes:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(1.\) That which is resorted to for the purpose of making a market for) Tj T*
(issues of new securities.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(2.\) That which is designed to serve merely speculative purposes in the) Tj T*
(endeavor to make a profit as the result of fluctuations which have been) Tj T*
(planned in advance.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The first kind of manipulation has certain advantages, and when not) Tj T*
(accompanied by ?matched orders? is unobjectionable _per se_. It is) Tj T*
(essential to the organization and carrying through of important) Tj T*
(enterprises, such as large corporations, that the organizers should be) Tj T*
(able to raise the money necessary to complete them. This can be done) Tj T*
(only by the sale of securities. Large blocks of securities, such as) Tj T*
(are frequently issued by railroad and other companies, cannot be sold) Tj T*
(over the counter or directly to the ultimate investor, whose confidence) Tj T*
(in them can, as a rule, be only gradually established. They must) Tj T*
(therefore, if sold at all, be disposed of to some syndicate, who will) Tj T*
(in turn pass them on to middlemen or speculators, until, in the course) Tj T*
(of time, they find their way into the boxes of investors. But prudent) Tj T*
(investors are not likely to be induced to buy securities which are not) Tj T*
(regularly quoted on some exchange, and which they cannot sell, or on) Tj T*
(which they cannot borrow money at their pleasure. If the securities) Tj T*
(are really good and bids and offers bona fide, open to all sellers and) Tj T*
(buyers, the operation is harmless. It is merely a method of bringing) Tj T*
(new investments into public notice.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The second kind of manipulation mentioned is undoubtedly open to) Tj T*
(serious criticism. It has for its object either the creation of high) Tj T*
(prices for particular stocks, in order to draw in the public as buyers) Tj T*
(and to unload upon them the holdings of the operators, or to depress) Tj T*
(the prices and induce the public to sell. There have been instances) Tj T*
(of gross and unjustifiable manipulation of securities, as in the case) Tj T*
(of American Ice stock. While we have been unable to discover any) Tj T*
(complete remedy short of abolishing the Stock Exchange itself, we are) Tj T*
(convinced that the Exchange can prevent the worst forms of this evil) Tj T*
(by exercising its influence and authority over the members to prevent) Tj T*
(them. When continued manipulation exists it is patent to experienced) Tj T*
