(this organization in published market reports, there are no actual) Tj T*
(sales on the floor of the Metal Exchange, and we are assured that there) Tj T*
(have been none for several years. Prices are, however, manipulated) Tj T*
(up and down by a quotation committee of three, chosen annually, who) Tj T*
(represent the great metal-selling agencies as their interest may) Tj T*
(appear, affording facilities for fixing prices on large contracts,) Tj T*
(mainly for the profit of a small clique, embracing, however, some of) Tj T*
(the largest interests in the metal trade.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(These practices result in deceiving buyers and sellers. The making and) Tj T*
(publishing of quotations for commodities or securities by groups of men) Tj T*
(calling themselves an exchange, or by any other similar title, whether) Tj T*
(incorporated or not, should be prohibited by law, where such quotations) Tj T*
(do not fairly and truthfully represent any bona fide transactions on) Tj T*
(such exchanges. Under present conditions, we are of the opinion that) Tj T*
(the Mercantile and Metal Exchanges do actual harm to producers and) Tj T*
(consumers, and that their charters should be repealed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THE EXPERIENCE OF GERMANY) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In 1892 a commission was appointed by the German Government to) Tj T*
(investigate the methods of the Berlin Exchange. The regular business) Tj T*
(of this exchange embraced both securities and commodities; it was an) Tj T*
(open board where anybody by paying a small fee could trade either for) Tj T*
(his own account, or as a broker. The broker could make such charge as) Tj T*
(he pleased for his services, there being no fixed rate of commission.) Tj T*
(Settlements took place monthly. Margins were not always required. Under) Tj T*
(these circumstances many undesirable elements gained entrance to the) Tj T*
(Exchange and some glaring frauds resulted.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The commission was composed of government officials, merchants,) Tj T*
(bankers, manufacturers, professors of political economy, and) Tj T*
(journalists. It was in session one year and seven months. Its report) Tj T*
(was completed in November, 1893. Although there had been a widespread) Tj T*
(popular demand that all short selling should be prohibited, the) Tj T*
(commission became satisfied that such a policy would be harmful to) Tj T*
(German trade and industry, and they so reported. They were willing,) Tj T*
(however, to prohibit speculation in industrial stocks. In general the) Tj T*
(report was conservative in tone.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THE LAW OF 1896) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Reichstag, however, rejected the bill recommended by the commission) Tj T*
